  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "And I, brethren, could not speak unto you as unto spiritual, but as unto carnal, even as unto babes in Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "I have fed you with milk, and not with meat: for hitherto ye were not able to bear it, neither yet now are ye able.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For ye are yet carnal: for whereas there is among you envying, and strife, and divisions, are ye not carnal, and walk as men?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For while one saith, I am of Paul; and another, I am of Apollos; are ye not carnal?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Who then is Paul, and who is Apollos, but ministers by whom ye believed, even as the Lord gave to every man?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "I have planted, Apollos watered; but God gave the increase.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "So then neither is he that planteth any thing, neither he that watereth; but God that giveth the increase.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Now he that planteth and he that watereth are one: and every man shall receive his own reward according to his own labour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For we are labourers together with God: ye are God’s husbandry, ye are God’s building.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "According to the grace of God which is given unto me, as a wise masterbuilder, I have laid the foundation, and another buildeth thereon. But let every man take heed how he buildeth thereupon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "For other foundation can no man lay than that is laid, which is Jesus Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Now if any man build upon this foundation gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, stubble;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Every man’s work shall be made manifest: for the day shall declare it, because it shall be revealed by fire; and the fire shall try every man’s work of what sort it is.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "If any man’s work abide which he hath built thereupon, he shall receive a reward.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "If any man’s work shall be burned, he shall suffer loss: but he himself shall be saved; yet so as by fire.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and that the Spirit of God dwelleth in you?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "If any man defile the temple of God, him shall God destroy; for the temple of God is holy, which temple ye are.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Let no man deceive himself. If any man among you seemeth to be wise in this world, let him become a fool, that he may be wise.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "For the wisdom of this world is foolishness with God. For it is written, He taketh the wise in their own craftiness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "And again, The Lord knoweth the thoughts of the wise, that they are vain.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Therefore let no man glory in men. For all things are yours;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Whether Paul, or Apollos, or Cephas, or the world, or life, or death, or things present, or things to come; all are yours;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "And ye are Christ’s; and Christ is God’s.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 3:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:3:23"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
